1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:06,298
You probably never noticed, but the WNBA ball is 1 inch smaller than the NBA ball.

2
00:00:06,298 --> 00:00:09,172
Why did a player in 1978 start that?

3
00:00:09,172 --> 00:00:12,905
NBA: size 7. WNBA: size 6,

4
00:00:12,905 --> 00:00:15,946
about an inch smaller and a couple of ounces lighter.

5
00:00:15,946 --> 00:00:19,909
In 1978, pro player Karen Logan suggested it,

6
00:00:19,909 --> 00:00:22,598
because on average, women's hands are smaller.

7
00:00:22,598 --> 00:00:25,755
If this already beats your trivia night, hit subscribe.

8
00:00:25,755 --> 00:00:27,636
It's free, and so is being right.

9
00:00:27,636 --> 00:00:29,948
College switched in 1984.

10
00:00:29,948 --> 00:00:32,379
The WNBA used it from day one.

11
00:00:32,379 --> 00:00:36,235
And by 2004, it was the rule for women worldwide.

12
00:00:36,235 --> 00:00:38,604
The twist? It wasn't based on science.

13
00:00:38,604 --> 00:00:40,827
It helped ball-handling, but not shooting.

14
00:00:40,827 --> 00:00:44,940
Should the WNBA keep the smaller ball?
